                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_25\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (sceAtracGetStreamDataInfo: fixed issue) modifies setHalfwayBuffer() in\nsrc/jpcsp/HLE/modules/sceAtrac3plus.java. Before the fix, the code unconditionally computed:\n\n    int maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap = bufferSize - ((bufferSize - info.inputFileDataOffset) % info.atracBytesPerFrame);\n    int maxSizeAfterFirstWrap = bufferSize - (bufferSize % info.atracBytesPerFrame);\n    inputBuffer = new pspFileBuffer(addr, maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap, maxSizeAfterFirstWrap, readSize, readSize);\n\nThe fix wraps this alignment logic in a conditional (`if (readSize < bufferSize) { ... }`), defaulting\nmaxSizeBeforeFirstWrap/maxSizeAfterFirstWrap to the plain bufferSize otherwise, and only applying the\nframe-aligned wrap sizes when the aligned size is still >= readSize. This shows that the unconditional\nalignment computation could produce an incorrect (too-small) buffer size whenever the buffer was\nalready fully read in (readSize == bufferSize) or when the aligned size ended up smaller than readSize,\ncausing corrupted stream/read-position tracking (surfacing in sceAtracGetStreamDataInfo).\n\nCandidate_25 is exactly the commit that introduced this unconditional alignment logic. Prior to\ncandidate_25 (see candidate_16, which contains the original/simple form), setHalfwayBuffer used:\n\n    inputBuffer = new pspFileBuffer(addr, bufferSize, readSize, readSize);\n\nCandidate_25 changed this to the buggy unconditional computation:\n\n    int maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap = bufferSize - ((bufferSize - info.inputFileDataOffset) % info.atracBytesPerFrame);\n    int maxSizeAfterFirstWrap = bufferSize - (bufferSize % info.atracBytesPerFrame);\n    inputBuffer = new pspFileBuffer(addr, maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap, maxSizeAfterFirstWrap, readSize, readSize);\n\nThis is verbatim the code removed by the fix (the \"-\" lines in fix_commit_diff.txt match candidate_25's\nadded \"+\" lines exactly), confirming candidate_25 is the bug-introducing commit. No intervening\ncandidate (candidate_34, which only adds logging/reinit guard changes) touches this logic, so the bug\npersisted unchanged from candidate_25 until the fix.\n"
                }
